$\begin{array}{llrl}
\text { Let } & & I=\int_2^3 \frac{\sqrt{x}}{\sqrt{5-x}+\sqrt{x}} d x \qquad \text{....(i)} \\
\therefore & & I=\int_2^3 \frac{\sqrt{5-x}}{\sqrt{x}+\sqrt{5-x}} d x \qquad \text{....(ii)} 
\end{array}
On adding Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get
$\begin{aligned}
2 I & =\int_2^{3 \sqrt{x}+\sqrt{5-x}} \frac{\sqrt{x}+\sqrt{5-x}}{} d x \\
& =\int_2^3 1 d x=3-2=1 \\
\Rightarrow \quad I & =\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}
